llm_calls.content:
{
  "selected_feature_id": 138,
  "rationale": "Public health coverage is a strong, semantically relevant proxy for low income and program eligibility that should remain predictive across domains. It adds household-need information not already captured by age, education, family structure, and work intensity, while being less domain-identifying and less brittle than state, year, race, ancestry, or place-of-birth features."
}

